            <ArticleTitle>Unusual exercise response associated with mitral regurgitation and ischemic heart disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>153-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient is presented with ischemic heart disease and mitral regurgitation; the patient's pulmonary artery wedge &quot;V&quot; waves and left ventricular end diastolic pressure decreased during exercise. Possible explanations for this unusual hemodynamic response are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
